ok - fm-t3-mcp login: PKCE sign-in writes a 0600 credential with the environment id and prints no secret
ok - fm-t3-mcp login: the origin defaults to FM_T3CODE_ORIGIN, then T3's runtime file, else refuses naming both
ok - fm-t3-mcp login: refuses every ceiling but full-access before any request
ok - fm-t3-mcp status: gate passes over JSON and SSE replies with the 2025-06-18 protocol header
ok - fm-t3-mcp gate: refuses a server missing a required tool or its identity tool
ok - fm-t3-mcp: refuses a server whose environment id differs from the credential's
ok - fm-t3-mcp credential: refuses expired, missing, and over-readable credentials, and warns before expiry
ok - fm-t3-mcp: a 401 from a revoked credential is a local refusal naming a fresh sign-in
ok - fm-t3-mcp projects: matched by real path, deleted ones skipped, a failed create resolves to a registered project, project-read returns the default model
ok - fm-t3-mcp launch: idle full-access thread on the existing worktree or the project root, with the given model selection
ok - fm-t3-mcp launch: refuses a binding T3 did not honor, reports a lost, unproven, or unarchived launch as uncertain, and a gate failure as no launch
ok - fm-t3-mcp thread verbs: idempotent send, state and turn time, bounded capture, interrupt claims, and proven archive
ok - fm-t3-mcp thread-for-root: only an unarchived, running, worktree-less thread on the root resolves
ok - fm-t3-mcp: tool errors exit 3 with T3's code, an unreachable server exits 1
ok - fm-t3-mcp status: reports telemetry off only when the server process proves it, and warns otherwise
ok - fm-t3-mcp read: --limit is capped at T3's own 100
ok - fm-t3-mcp interrupt: confirmation waits on exactly the run T3 interrupted, never a later run
ok - fm-t3-mcp send: a reply lost after commit exits 7, and the same-id retry lands as one delivery
ok - fm-t3-mcp session-stop: refused on upstream T3, replayed by id on the fork, and unproven on a lost reply or a live run
ok - fm-t3-mcp keep-alive: refused on upstream T3, proven by T3's update result on the fork, repeatable, and never pins a worker
ok - fm-t3-mcp thread-for-root: every page is read, forks count, subagents do not
ok - fm-t3-mcp resolve-selection: driver, model, and options come from T3's catalog; an effort override keeps other options
ok - fm-t3-mcp resolve-selection: a catalog that lists option values as a values array is read like the older options list
ok - fm-t3-mcp: the launch schema's environment property gates pi and --environment; values are checked against T3's limits before any launch
ok - fm-t3-mcp launch: the configuration read-back must show the instance, model, and every requested option
ok - fm-t3-mcp requests/respond: questions are read and answered by id; approvals are counted, never answered
ok - fm-t3-mcp gate: each merged capability is met by the T3 0.1.3 tool or the complete earlier family
ok - fm-t3-mcp current tools: launch read-back and pending requests use t3_thread_configure and t3_pending_request
ok - fm-t3-mcp gate: with both generations offered, the configuration read stays on the dedicated tool and pending requests use the merged tool
ok - fm-t3-mcp watch: exact-run waits end on a terminal run, idle threads never wait, and pending requests block once per signature
ok - fm-t3-mcp watch: waits that all fail are an error, not a timeout
ok - fm-t3-mcp: a helper reached through a symlinked path runs its verb instead of exiting silently
ok - fm-t3-mcp: an empty reply is never success: a send stays unconfirmed and a read fails
ok - fm-t3-mcp watch: each pending approval is identified, so one answered and replaced between watches escalates again
ok - fm-t3-mcp: a JSON-RPC server error after a send or launch is unconfirmed, never a proven refusal
ok - fm-t3-mcp: T3's orchestration_error, or a tool error without a code, after a send or launch is unconfirmed; a specific typed refusal stays proven
ok - fm-t3-mcp wait: a long wait re-arms in slices under Node's 300 s reply limit
ok - fm-t3-mcp capture: --lines above 500 reads the last 500, and the verb ends its MCP session
